@startuml
title scenario Process Al Fouad Transaction Job

start

:System initiates or retries transaction event;
note left
  Handles 2 retry types correctly:
  1. Payment Retry: transaction has status Failed and the
     user retries the payment it belongs to.
  2. Queue Retry: the worker crashed / timed out mid-job
     and the processor picks up the same job again.
  Transaction is set to 'waiting' here so it is not retried
  while we are about to create it at Al Fouad.
end note

:System reads Al Fouad request identity
(account, branch, username, password, public key)
from the program FSP configuration;

:System looks for an existing alfouad_transaction
for this transactionId whose status is null;
note left
  Recovers an in-flight transaction after a crash or a
  timeout during create, so we reuse its ReferenceNumber
  instead of creating a second transaction.
end note

if (Existing transaction with status = null?) then (no)
  :System counts failed transaction attempts
   for this transactionId;
  :System generates ReferenceNumber;
  note right
    ReferenceNumber = generateUUIDFromSeed(
      referenceId + transactionId + failedTransactionAttempts)
    - Payment Retry: attempts++ -> NEW reference.
    - Queue Retry: same attempts -> SAME reference, so
      Al Fouad answers 822 and we reconcile the existing one.
  end note
  :System stores alfouad_transaction
   (ReferenceNumber, status = null);
else (yes)
  :System reuses the stored ReferenceNumber;
endif

:System authenticates and calls
 Al Fouad TransactionCreate;
note right: RSA-encrypted password inside a Base64 <Authentication> Bearer token.

switch (Outcome?)
case (State=1 success)
  :System stores TransactionUID and sets status = created;
  :System leaves transaction on 'waiting'
   and creates a success transaction event;

case (State=0, 822 duplicate or timeout)
  :System calls TransactionByRef
   with the same ReferenceNumber;
  if (Transaction found at Al Fouad?) then (yes)
    :System stores TransactionUID and maps lifecycle state
     (Paid=3 -> success, Canceled=5 -> error, 1/2/4 -> waiting);
    :System leaves transaction on 'waiting'
     and creates a success transaction event;
  else (no)
    if (Reason was 822 duplicate?) then (yes - inconsistent)
      :Duplicate reported but reference not found:
       set transaction 'error' and raise an alert;
    else (timeout - not created)
      :System leaves status = null and transaction on 'waiting';
      note right
        Reconciliation / the next attempt reuses the SAME
        ReferenceNumber to create it (no self-requeue,
        no infinite loop).
      end note
    endif
  endif

case (State=0, other error e.g. 45)
  :System sets alfouad_transaction status = failed;
  :System updates transaction to 'error'
   and creates related event;
endswitch

:System updates Redis in-progress set;
stop
@enduml